cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use polyband in work you publish, please cite it."
title: polyband
abstract: >-
  A polynomial regression that determines two curves at once: the mean
  relation running through a scatter plot, and the envelope describing how
  wide the scatter around it is. The trend is a polynomial in x and the
  logarithm of the width is a second, independent polynomial in x; both are
  fitted simultaneously by maximum likelihood, so the trend is automatically
  weighted by the local scatter. Supports measurement errors, log-space
  fitting, and a Student-t likelihood that bounds the influence of outliers
  on the trend and on the envelope alike.
